  "question": {
    "text": "The current in an inductor is given by $\\mathrm{I}=(3 \\mathrm{t}+8)$ where $\\mathrm{t}$ is in second. The magnitude of induced emf produced in the inductor is $12 \\mathrm{mV}$. The self-inductance of the inductor _____ $\\mathrm{mH}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{I}=3 \\mathrm{t}+8 \\\\ & \\varepsilon=12 \\mathrm{mV} \\\\ & |\\varepsilon|=\\mathrm{L}\\left|\\frac{\\mathrm{dI}}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right| \\\\ & 12=\\mathrm{L} \\times 3 \\\\ & \\mathrm{~L}=4 \\mathrm{mH}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
